# The Sacred Shrine Clearing

You find a hidden clearing deep in the forest. Ancient stone pillars form a circle around a moss-covered altar. The air here feels different -- charged with old magic.

The image shows the mountain landscape visible through a break in the canopy above -- a reminder that there is a world beyond this dark forest.

<<if $quest_artifact == "active" and not $amulet_recovered>>
### The Altar

At the center of the clearing sits a stone altar. Upon it rests a small, ancient amulet -- a disc of tarnished silver with a glowing green stone at its center. It pulses with a faint light, matching the eerie lights reported in the forest.

This is the ''Amulet of Thornwood'' -- the artifact Mara's husband died seeking.

[[Take the amulet|Take Amulet]]
[[Examine the altar more closely|Examine Altar]]
[[Leave it for now|Forest Entrance]]
<<else>>
The clearing is peaceful now. The amulet is gone -- in your possession or returned to Mara, the shrine's magic has calmed.

The clearing offers a moment of respite.

[[Meditate and recover HP|Shrine Meditation]]
[[Return to the forest entrance|Forest Entrance]]
<</if>>
